      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- TIP_DETAIL\n\n## Column Mapping\n- current academic term: ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.IS_CURRENT_TERM\n- term code: ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- number of subjects offered: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- total subject enrollment number: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- department with the highest number of subjects offered: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- count of subjects from that department: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each academic term that is marked as the current term, list the term code, term description, academic year, and the number of subjects offered along with the total subject enrollment number for that term.\n```sql\nSELECT atp.TERM_CODE, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, COUNT(ss.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, SUM(ss.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) AS total_enrollment FROM ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER atp JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON atp.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE WHERE atp.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y' GROUP BY atp.TERM_CODE, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR;\n```\n2. For each academic year, give the academic year description and calculate the average, range, and variance of the record counts for TIP materials in that year, considering only terms where the term status is not null and the TIP material status is not 'NM'.\n```sql\nSELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, AVG(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS avg_record_count, MAX(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) - MIN(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS record_count_range, VARIANCE(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS record_count_variance FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS ON ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE = ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE JOIN TIP_DETAIL ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE WHERE ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_STATUS IS NOT NULL AND TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM' GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC ORDER BY record_count_range DESC;\n```\n3. For each current academic term, list the term code, term description, academic year, the number of subjects offered, the total subject enrollment number for that term, the academic year description, and for that academic year, the average, range, and variance of the record counts for TIP materials (considering only terms where the term status is not null and the TIP material status is not 'NM'). Present the columns in the following order: term code, term description, academic year, subject count, total enrollment, academic year description, average record count, record count range, and record count variance.\n```sql\nWITH CurrentTermSubjects AS ( SELECT atp.TERM_CODE, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, COUNT(ss.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, SUM(ss.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) AS total_enrollment FROM ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER atp JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON atp.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE WHERE atp.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y' GROUP BY atp.TERM_CODE, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR ), AcademicYearTipStats AS ( SELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, AVG(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS avg_record_count, MAX(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) - MIN(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS record_count_range, VARIANCE(TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT) AS record_count_variance FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS ON ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE = ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE JOIN TIP_DETAIL ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE WHERE ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_STATUS IS NOT NULL AND TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM' GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC ORDER BY record_count_range DESC ), CombinedAcademicStats AS ( SELECT cts.TERM_CODE, cts.TERM_DESCRIPTION, cts.ACADEMIC_YEAR, cts.subject_count, cts.total_enrollment, ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, ays.avg_record_count, ays.record_count_range, ays.record_count_variance FROM CurrentTermSubjects cts JOIN AcademicYearTipStats ays ON cts.ACADEMIC_YEAR = ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR ) SELECT TERM_CODE, TERM_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_YEAR, subject_count, total_enrollment, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, avg_record_count, record_count_range, record_count_variance FROM CombinedAcademicStats ORDER BY TERM_CODE;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each current academic term, list the term code, term description, academic year, the number of subjects offered, the total subject enrollment number for that term, the academic year description, and for that academic year, the department with the highest number of subjects offered and the count of subjects from that department. Present the columns in the following order: term code, term description, academic year, subject count, total enrollment, academic year description, most prominent department, and department subject count. Do not return any rounded answers."
