FFER_DEPT_NAME, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) vs COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (catalog attributes, no enrollment). The column mapping explicitly anchors all four measures to SUBJECT_SUMMARY; concept_subject_offering_facts decision guide assigns \"final enrollment statistics … by department\" to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n\n| Requirement | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| subjects offered count (SUBJECT_ID) | SUPPORTED (mapping + columns) | SUPPORTED (has SUBJECT_ID) but not mapped | SUPPORTED but catalog-scope |\n| total subject enrollment (SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) | SUPPORTED (mapping; column exists) | has column but not mapped | NOT-SUPPORTED (no enrollment — concept matrix) |\n| department name for top-department | SUPPORTED (DEPARTMENT_NAME, mapping) | OFFER_DEPT_NAME (different convention) | DEPARTMENT_NAME |\n| current-term filter via TERM_CODE join | SUPPORTED (dw_4683 precedent) | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"current academic term\" → `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y'` (hint mapping; concept decision guide for relative-term resolution).\n- \"term description\" → `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_DESCRIPTION` (mapping lists it under ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER).\n- \"academic year\" / \"academic year description\" → `ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR` / `ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC` (mapping).\n- \"number of subjects offered\" → `COUNT(SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID)`; \"total subject enrollment number\" → `SUM(SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER)` (mapping).\n- \"department with the highest number of subjects offered … for that academic year\" → per-year ranking over `SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME` counts, year attached via TERM_CODE→ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (widest term coverage per decision guide; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL is a gold table).\n- \"for that academic year\" scope: the top-department computation spans ALL terms of the academic year (not just the current term), matching the sibling decomposition pattern where year-level stats are computed independently then joined on ACADEMIC_YEAR.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Current-term + SUBJECT_SUMMARY shape: dw_4683 (1 precedent, exact join chain `atp→at→ss` with `IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`).\n- \"Top department by count + count\" shape: dw_3042 (ROW_NUMBER rn=1 pattern), dw_2461 (\"most prominent department, count of subjects from that department\" phrasing).\n- Year-level aggregation over ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL joined to a fact table: hint sibling decomposition subquery 2 and dw_4231 (ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL for year attributes).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER: consumed by 17 metrics to resolve \"current/previous/upcoming term\"; always joined onward via TERM_CODE.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS: term status/regular-term filtering and academic-year enrichment of subject facts (dw_3417, dw_4683).\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: year-attribute source over widest coverage (dw_4231, sibling decomposition).\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY: enrollment/unit statistics by department & term (dw_4683, dw_4197, dw_3644).\n- TIP_DETAIL: textbook-material statistics — no role in this question's output columns.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER — semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓, metrics_by_table ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS — semantic_get ✓, graph (via neighbors of the other two) ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL — semantic_get ✓, graph ✓\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY — semantic_get ✓, graph neighbors ✓\n- TIP_DETAIL — semantic_get ✓ (excluded from query: no mapped output column)\n- concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts — semantic_get ✓\n- column_concept_term_code, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_enrollment_measures — semantic_get ✓; column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_year_columns, column_concept_master_subject_id — retrieved via search desc and graph membership ✓\n- Metrics dw_4683, dw_4231, dw_3042, dw_2461 — semantic_get (full SQL) ✓\n- mysql_query — attempted 7 times; all failed with server-side \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" (infrastructure outage, not a SQL error). Data verification could not be performed; the SQL follows exactly the verified gold-shape precedents.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER (`TERM_CODE`, `TERM_DESCRIPTION`, `IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`) → ACADEMIC_TERMS (`ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`) → SUBJECT_SUMMARY (`SUBJECT_ID` count, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` sum) for the term-level block; SUBJECT_SUMMARY joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL via TERM_CODE for the year-level top-department block (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)`, ROW_NUMBER rn=1 per dw_3042 precedent).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** two CTEs joined on ACADEMIC_YEAR; term-level GROUP BY term code/description/year/year-desc; year-level two-step aggregation (count per year+department, then rank, keep rank 1); final SELECT in the exact asked column order; ORDER BY TERM_CODE (per hint precedent). No rounding applied.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** Data — SUBJECT_SUMMARY is one row per subject per term with both required measures and DEPARTMENT_NAME; term tables are 1-row-per-term so no fan-out; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL guarantees year coverage for all SUBJECT_SUMMARY terms. Semantic-network — concept decision guides explicitly route \"current term\" to ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER, official enrollment to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, summary-analysis department to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, and widest year coverage to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL. Business — dw_4683 is an exact current-term/SUBJECT_SUMMARY precedent; dw_3042/dw_2461 are exact \"top department + its count\" precedents.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY could count subjects but lacks the mapped enrollment column semantics and department naming convention; TIP_DETAIL is a gold-table leftover from the sibling question with no mapped output column here — including it would alter results without any wording support.\n\n",
